    "name": "Project Setup",
    "alias": "Project Configuration",
    "icon": "settings_applications",
    "tagline": "Configure a project's work structure, people, cost, schedule, forms, and safety/quality/drawing setup before field execution begins.",
    "color": "#8a5a3c",
    "overview": "<p>Project Setup is the foundational configuration module a construction business works through before a project goes live in the field. Across fourteen tabs — Works, Tasks, People, Estimate, Schedule, Phase Codes, Quality, Safety, Drawings, Documents, Workorder, Forms, BIM, and GIS — a PM or Module Admin defines the project's work breakdown, staffs it, budgets and schedules it, and configures the forms, approval workflows, and document structures that Field Works will run against day to day. It is overwhelmingly a PM/Module Admin space: the setup layer that has to be right before End Users ever open a form, log time, or submit an inspection in the field.</p>",
    "navigation": [
      "Open a <strong>Project</strong>, then use the Project Setup tab bar to move between Works, Tasks, People, Estimate, Schedule, Phase Codes, Quality, Safety, Drawings, Documents, Workorder, Forms, BIM, and GIS.",
      "Several tabs (People, Estimate, Quality, Safety, Drawings, Documents, Forms) have their own sub-tabs; Forms goes one level further with a three-level category → sub-area → form-type navigation."
    ],
